===Etymology 1===
{{affix|en|kick|-er|id2=agent noun}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[kick|kicks]].
# {{lb|en|sports}} One who takes kicks.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[kicking strap]].
# {{lb|en|nautical|informal}} An [[outboard motor]].
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} An unexpected [[situation]], [[detail]] or circumstance, often [[unpleasant]].
#: ''John wants to climb the wall, but the '''kicker''' is that it is thirty feet tall.''
#: ''Tuition is free; the '''kicker''' is that mandatory room and board costs twice as much as at other colleges.''
# {{lb|en|finance}} An enticement for investors, e.g. [[warranty]] added to the investment contract.
# {{lb|en|poker}} An [[unpaired]] [[card]] which is part of a [[pair]], [[two pair]], or [[three of a kind]] poker hand.
#: ''Jill's hand was two pair, aces and sevens, with a king '''kicker'''.''
# {{lb|en|journalism}} The last one or two paragraphs of a story.
# {{lb|en|journalism}} {{synonym of|lead-in|lang=en|gloss=start of photo caption}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[launch ramp]].

