===Etymology 2===
The southern-U.S. sense referring to a person derives from {{m|en|shit-kicker}}, referring to a cowboy with boots used to kick away cow manure.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang|Southern US}} A particular type of [[Texan]] who is associated with [[country]]/[[western]] attire, attitudes{{,}} and/or philosophy.

